---
import Layout from '../../components/layout/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL } from '../../config';
import { GA4_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';

const title = 'Privacy Policy - GDPR Compliance and Data Protection';
const description = 'Privacy policy: your salary never leaves your browser. Audience measured with Google Analytics cookies, no advertising; cookieless Clarity checks site stability.';

const schemas = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: '/en/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/en/privacy-policy/' },
  ]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} schema={schemas} locale="en">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-8">
    <nav class="mb-6 text-sm text-medium-gray">
      <a href="/en/" class="hover:text-brand">Home</a> / <span class="text-charcoal dark:text-gray-200">Privacy Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold text-charcoal md:text-4xl dark:text-gray-100">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none text-dark-gray dark:text-gray-300 space-y-6">
      <p><em>Last updated: October {new Date().getFullYear()}</em></p>

      <p>
        This privacy policy explains how {SITE_NAME} ({SITE_URL}) handles your personal data in compliance
        with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR, Regulation EU 2016/679) and the Spanish Organic
        Law 3/2018 on Personal Data Protection and Digital Rights (LOPDGDD).
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">1. Data Controller</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Controller:</strong> Radif Partners</li>
        <li><strong>Website:</strong> {SITE_URL}</li>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@elsueldoneto.es" class="text-brand hover:underline">contact@elsueldoneto.es</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The data controller is the entity that determines the purposes and means of the processing of
        personal data, in accordance with Article 4(7) of the GDPR.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">2. Data Protection Officer</h2>
      <p>
        Given the nature of the website and the absence of large-scale processing of personal data, the
        appointment of a Data Protection Officer (DPO) is not legally required under Article 37 of the GDPR.
        Should processing circumstances change, the controller will appoint a DPO and publish the relevant
        contact details.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">3. What You Type Stays in Your Browser</h2>
      <p>
        The net salary,
        IRPF, severance and pension calculators run entirely in your browser: the gross salary, autonomous
        community, family situation or contract type you enter is never sent to a server, never saved in a
        database and is gone once you close the page. What you type is not stored on your device; the
        only cookies on the site are the Google Analytics audience measurement cookies (section 4).
      </p>
      <p>
        This follows the "privacy by design" principle of Article 25 GDPR: there are no user accounts, no
        forms that store data and no newsletter. If you e-mail us, we keep your message and address only as
        long as needed to reply.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">4. Audience Measurement with Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The site uses <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to count visits and see which pages are useful: pages
        viewed, referring page, visit length, device and browser type, approximate country and city. To do so
        Google Analytics sets two cookies on your device: <code>_ga</code>, which tells visitors apart with a
        random identifier, and <code>_ga_{GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code>, which keeps the state of the visit. Their
        lifetime is set to 13 months at most (390 days) and is not extended on each visit; Google’s default is
        2 years.
      </p>
      <p>
        The IP address is anonymised: Google Analytics 4 neither logs nor stores it, and only uses it at
        collection time to derive an approximate country and city. The page address sent to Google Analytics is
        stripped of its parameters, so amounts carried by a share link are not included. The site shows no
        advertising: ad storage, ad user data, ad personalisation and Google signals are switched off, and
        measurement data is shared with no advertiser.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Provider:</strong> Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland, acting as processor (Article 28 GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> audience measurement.</li>
        <li><strong>Retention at Google:</strong> 14 months, then deletion.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> the publisher’s legitimate interest in knowing how its site is used (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Objecting:</strong> block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="text-brand hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. The site works the same way.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">5. Technical Stability Measurement with Microsoft Clarity</h2>
      <p>
        To detect errors, slow pages, clicks with no effect or scrolling issues, the site uses
        <strong>Microsoft Clarity without cookies</strong>. The page signals to Clarity that storage is denied
        before its script loads, so it sets no <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or
        <code>CLID</code> cookie, uses a fresh identifier for every page view and does not connect your visits.
        Page text and the amounts you type are masked in your browser before sending. Apart from Google
        Analytics and Clarity, there is no advertising and no other tracker.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Controller for this measurement:</strong> Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland (<a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" class="text-brand hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy statement</a>).</li>
        <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> technical stability of the site only.</li>
        <li><strong>Retention:</strong> 30 days for recordings, at most 13 months for aggregated figures.</li>
        <li><strong>Opting out:</strong> block <code>clarity.ms</code> in your browser, or write to us.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        More in our <a href="/en/cookie-policy/" class="text-brand hover:underline">cookie policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">6. Legal Basis</h2>
      <p>
        Audience measurement and stability measurement rely on the publisher’s legitimate interest
        (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR) in knowing how the site is used and keeping the calculators working; no consent
        is requested and no banner is shown. Replying to an e-mail relies on your own request.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">7. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Articles 15 to 22 of the GDPR and the LOPDGDD you have rights of access, rectification, erasure,
        restriction, portability and objection. With no user accounts we usually hold no data that identifies
        you, apart from e-mails you have sent us; for Google Analytics, the simplest objection is in section 4. Write to contact@elsueldoneto.es; we reply within 30 days (Article 12 GDPR).
        You may also lodge a complaint with the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD) at
        <a href="https://www.aepd.es" class="text-brand hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aepd.es</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">8. Hosting and Server Logs</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by OVH SAS (2 rue Kellermann, 59100 Roubaix, France), whose servers automatically
        log IP address, date and requested page for security purposes, for a short period.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">9. Transfers Outside the EU</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics data may be transferred to Google LLC, and Clarity measurements processed on Microsoft
        servers, both in the United States, under the
        EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">10. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        Our website is served over a secure HTTPS connection that encrypts all data in transit. Appropriate
        technical and organizational measures are implemented in accordance with Article 32 of the GDPR to
        ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">11. Changes and Contact</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to update this privacy policy to reflect changes in our practices or applicable
        law. The current version is always available on this page. For questions or to exercise your rights,
        contact us at:<br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:contact@elsueldoneto.es" class="text-brand hover:underline">contact@elsueldoneto.es</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
